cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this manuscript, model, or the accompanying code, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Yurov"
    given-names: "D. V."
title: "Model MEML 75: Quark and lepton mass matrices from mixed T^2/Z_3 x T^2/Z_4 geometry with axion-like dark matter and leptogenesis"
version: 24.5.5
date-released: "2026-11-14"
abstract: >-
  Model MEML 75 is a phenomenological construction that parametrizes the fermion sector of the Standard Model 
  through mixed six-dimensional orbifolds. The model has 13 fitted parameters for 16 observables (N_dof = +3 or +4) 
  and 5 postulates. It yields testable consequences for axion-like dark matter (f_a = 1.98e11 GeV, m_a = 28.4 ueV), 
  neutrino masses, and leptogenesis (conditional on a curvaton). We honestly report twelve documented negative results, 
  including the failure of pure GVW to stabilize moduli and the failure to structurally derive c_d, c_1, c_2 from modular forms. 
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24227241"
  The model makes zero independent predictions; all observables are fitted or postdicted.
